        {
          "kind": "creation_and_submission_timing",
          "questionToResolve": "Reconcile the after-initial-submission initiation statement with the supplied evidence about creation before initial submission. Distinguish creation from submission; explain whether the sources actually reconcile or leave a creation-timing question unresolved. Retain a source-stated submission limit in its applicable scope. A dated release is evidence of that release's behavior, not proof that current conflicting guidance is superseded.",
          "evidence": {
            "sourceID": "dob-subsequent-faq",
            "claimID": "official-passage-77183aa15dad687a6565894d",
            "contentHash": "ce6d0104578e5fbf53f716249cd0047ba2c135a78bff42ede2ef273eddae44fe",
            "excerpts": [
              "Subsequent filings can be initiated and submitted after the initial job filing is submitted (not in pre-filing status).",
              "Fields from the subsequent filing are populated from the initial filing (I1). The fields will not update on the subsequent filing until the I1 is submitted. To prevent this issue, we recommend completing as much of the I1 as possible before creating the subsequent filing.",
              "A subsequent filing can be submitted anytime until an LOC has been issued for the initial filing."
            ]
          },
          "relatedEvidence": [
            {
              "sourceID": "dob-build-release-notes",
              "claimID": "official-passage-da970df54086b0ddac95a601",
              "contentHash": "03c2b6c9eac3f540be3911f8813b3e1a3591c25f78c7bc721d19d3ce3678b9e0",
              "excerpts": [
                "Create a subsequent filing when an initial filing is in pre - filing status . Subsequent filings can be submitted only after the initial filing is submitted."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "filing_completion_scope",
          "questionToResolve": "The chosen filing path has separate processing and a job-type-dependent completion consequence. Reconcile the general separate-LOC direction with the specialized NB/Alteration-CO initial-CO path. State the branches briefly and identify the initial job type if unknown; do not drop the completion consequence while explaining which filing to use.",
          "evidence": {
            "sourceID": "dob-application-guide",
            "claimID": "official-passage-789cc7ccd439eb8374132031",
            "contentHash": "9befc1cc76dd0efbfb76fed2960c262f1c4a61fc8dd786f9c30341251cc852b5",
            "excerpts": [
              "a Letter of Completion (LOC) is requested separately on each filing."
            ]
          },
          "relatedEvidence": [
            {
              "sourceID": "dob-nb-altco-faq",
              "claimID": "official-passage-42b3262068b7a32078d4c986",
              "contentHash": "b5d4f1834964f64fb25bb7a5c31746d2131ccf70f9f7885b5003d54e07d9e92e",
              "excerpts": [
                "Do I need to request a Letter of Completion for the subsequent filing of an NB or Alteration-CO filing? — No, the status of the subsequent filings will remain Permit Entire. Only the status of the initial (I1) filing will change to CO issued."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
